<title>JAPAN: Japan 1996 lead battery sales edge up 0.6 pct.</title>
<headline>Japan 1996 lead battery sales edge up 0.6 pct.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-01-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's sales of domestic lead batteries, measured in volume of contained lead, rose a marginal 0.6 percent in 1996 from the year before to 268,303 tonnes, the Japan Storage Battery Association said on Friday.</p>
<p>Contained lead in Japanese battery sales in December was (in tonnes):</p>
<p>			1996	  yr/yr change</p>
<p> Total	     268,303	 +0.6 pct</p>
<p>   Automotive    207,239	 -1.4 pct</p>
<p>   Industrial     42,309	+13.6 pct</p>
<p>(NOTE: Automotive includes a small quantity of lead used in two-wheeled vehicles. Industrial use includes stationary power sources and electric vehicles such as forklifts.)</p>
<p>Unit shipments of Japanese car batteries (in 1,000s):</p>
<p>			 1996	 yr/yr change</p>
<p> TOTAL		24,303	 -1.2 pct</p>
<p> Domestic	   23,613	 -0.9 pct</p>
<p>   New cars	 11,077	 +2.5 pct</p>
<p>   Replacement    12,535	 -3.7 pct</p>
<p> Exports		 690	-10.3 pct</p>
<p>(NOTE: Unit shipment data excludes two-wheeled vehicles.)</p>
<p>--Tokyo Commodity Desk +81-3-3432-6179</p>
</text>
